---
/**
 * /services: Room IV, Commissions. The one page that sells scrollies
 * (visualized essays, poems, stories) and nothing else. Built from the
 * museum's own parts: the placard, the Room I feature-list cells, the
 * Gallery cards (six live pieces, their own share images as thumbnails),
 * the meander and the colophon, and the ten questions (IV.05) whose answers
 * also feed the FAQPage JSON-LD. The close (IV.06) embeds the BackGold intake
 * form once SCROLLY_INTAKE_URL is set. No script beyond what Museum.astro loads.
 */
import Museum from '../layouts/Museum.astro';
import Placard from '../components/museum/Placard.astro';
import PoemGallery from '../components/museum/PoemGallery.astro';
import Meander from '../components/museum/Meander.astro';
import Colophon from '../components/museum/Colophon.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SCHEDULER_URL, SCROLLY_INTAKE_URL, SITE_URL } from '../config/site';

const url = `${SITE_URL}/services/`;
const mailto = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Commission')}`;

const jobs = [
  {
    title: 'An essay or poem of your own',
    body: 'Your writing given the treatment the gallery pieces get: exhibits built for the argument, Greek or any other language set correctly, a source ledger if the piece makes claims.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Impact report',
    body: 'For nonprofits and foundations. The year’s work as a page donors actually finish: the numbers drawn as you reach them, the people in the middle of it, the ask at the end. Replaces the PDF nobody opens.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Launch page',
    body: 'For authors, musicians, and artists. A chapter, a track, or a series given its own interactive page, with a pre-order or ticket door built into the scroll.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Origin story',
    body: 'For founders. How the company came to be, told the way you tell it in the room, with the product arriving where it arrives in the story. Doubles as the pitch page.',
  },
];

const steps = [
  {
    title: 'The story session',
    body: 'An hour on what happened and why it matters. I leave with the spine of the piece and a chapter outline you approve.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The exhibits',
    body: 'Each chapter gets its own exhibit: a drawing, a chart, a wall of files, a flood. You review a working prototype on desktop and phone.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The build and the twin',
    body: 'The page ships with a plain-text twin for sharing and search, a share image rendered from the page itself, and a source ledger where the piece makes claims.',
  },
];


/* IV.05 · Questions. The copy is the owner's, verbatim; the FAQPage
   JSON-LD below is built from this same array so the schema can never
   disagree with the visible text. */
const faq = [
  {
    q: 'What is a scrolly?',
    a: 'A scrolly is a long piece told as a web page where the design is part of the argument. As you scroll, a pinned exhibit changes state, a chart draws itself when you reach it, a held button turns the page. Newsrooms call them scrollytelling; I build them for essays, poems, reports, and founders\u2019 stories.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does a scrolly cost?',
    a: 'A scrolly starts at $2,500. The base price covers a piece of six to nine chapters with custom exhibits, a plain-text twin, a share image rendered from the page, and a source ledger where the piece makes claims. Longer pieces, original illustration, data cleaning, and voice or sound are quoted on the call. Half to start, half at launch.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does a scrolly take?',
    a: 'Three to five weeks from the story session to launch for a base piece. Week one is the spine and chapter outline you approve; weeks two and three are the exhibits and a working prototype on desktop and phone; the last stretch is the build, the twin, and your review. Larger pieces are scheduled on the call.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need data to commission a scrolly?',
    a: 'No. Most of the pieces in my gallery are built from a text, a myth, or a story, with the exhibits drawn to carry the argument. If you have data, it becomes a chart the reader reaches at the right moment; if you have none, the exhibits are drawings, documents, and instruments the reader handles.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does a scrolly work on a phone?',
    a: 'Yes. I read on a phone, so every piece is designed for the phone first and the desktop second. Pinned exhibits stack so the picture stays visible during the step that changes it, touch targets are sized for thumbs, and nothing depends on hover.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does a scrolly work with scripts off or with a screen reader?',
    a: 'Yes. Every piece ships with a plain-text twin: the full text in reading order, with each exhibit described in a sentence. A reader with scripts blocked, a screen reader, or a reduced-motion setting gets the whole argument. Search engines and AI assistants read that same version.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who owns the files?',
    a: 'You do. At launch you receive the source, the built page, the twin, and the share image, and you may host them anywhere. If I host the piece on my domain, you can move it at any time. Nothing is held back and nothing is licensed back to you.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can a scrolly live on my own domain?',
    a: 'Yes. A scrolly can be hosted on your domain, on a subdomain of it, or on mine with a link from your site. Hosting on your domain is the default for impact reports and origin stories; hosting on mine suits a single essay or poem that wants a gallery around it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is epistemic tagging?',
    a: 'Epistemic tagging marks every claim in a piece as text, reading, or disputed. \u201cText\u201d means the source says it; \u201creading\u201d means I am interpreting; \u201cdisputed\u201d means scholars disagree. A filterable ledger at the end lists every claim with its tag and source, so a reader can check the argument instead of taking it on faith.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you build an impact report, a launch page, or an origin story?',
    a: 'Yes. Those are the three commissions I build most, alongside essays and poems. An impact report tells a year\u2019s work as a page donors finish; a launch page gives a chapter, track, or series its own interactive home with a door built in; an origin story tells how a company came to be, product arriving where it arrives in the telling.',
  },
];

const pieces = [
  'mimics-and-mythmakers',
  'everyone-searchable',
  'true-amazons',
  'the-dual-thing',
  'pharmakon',
  'the-pretty-toy',
];

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Service',
    '@id': `${url}#service`,
    url,
    name: 'Commission a scrolly',
    serviceType: 'Visualized essays, poems, impact reports, launch pages and origin stories as interactive pages',
    description:
      'A story told as an interactive page: visualized essays, poems, impact reports, launch pages and origin stories, written with you and built by Michael Wilhelm.',
    provider: { '@type': 'Person', '@id': `${SITE_URL}/#person`, name: 'Michael Wilhelm', url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
    offers: {
      '@type': 'Offer',
      url,
      price: '2500',
      priceCurrency: 'USD',
      priceSpecification: {
        '@type': 'PriceSpecification',
        price: '2500',
        priceCurrency: 'USD',
        minPrice: '2500',
        description: 'From $2,500. Larger pieces quoted.',
      },
      availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock',
      offeredBy: { '@id': `${SITE_URL}/#person` },
    },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    '@id': `${url}#faq`,
    url,
    mainEntity: faq.map(({ q, a }) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
    })),
  },
];
---

<Museum
  title="Commission a Scrolly | Michael Wilhelm"
  description="A story told as an interactive page: visualized essays, poems, impact reports, launch pages and origin stories, written with you and built by Michael Wilhelm. From $2,500."
  current="services"
  schema={schema}
>
  <article class="page" aria-labelledby="services-title" style="--room-accent: var(--room-iv)">
    <div class="page__inner wrap">
      <header class="page__head">
        <Placard
          id="services-title"
          level={1}
          label="Room IV · Commissions"
          title="Pieces like these are built to order."
          medium="Visualized essays, poems and stories, written with you and built as their own interactive page"
          catalog="Cat. IV"
        />
        <div class="page__statement" data-reveal>
          <p class="lede">
            A scrolly is a long piece told as a page where the design is part of the plot: the text darkens as the
            argument does, a chart draws itself when you reach it, a held button turns the page. I write it with you,
            design the exhibit, and build it so it works on a phone, with the script off, and for a reader who cannot
            see motion.
          </p>
          <p class="actions">
            <a class="cta cta--gilt" href={SCHEDULER_URL}>Book a call</a>
            <a class="text-link actions__mail" href={mailto}>or write: {CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="sect" aria-labelledby="jobs-title" data-reveal>
        <div class="sect__head">
          <p class="sect__num mono">IV.01</p>
          <h2 class="sect__title display" id="jobs-title">Four jobs it does.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="cells" role="list">
          {
            jobs.map((j, i) => (
              <li class="cell">
                <span class="cell__num mono">IV.01.{i + 1}</span>
                <h3 class="cell__title">{j.title}</h3>
                <p class="cell__body">{j.body}</p>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="sect sect--wide" aria-labelledby="pieces-title" data-reveal>
        <div class="sect__head">
          <p class="sect__num mono">IV.02</p>
          <h2 class="sect__title display" id="pieces-title">Every one of these is live. Open any of them and scroll.</h2>
        </div>
        <PoemGallery level={3} ids={pieces} thumbs />
        <p class="more">
          <a class="text-link" href="/gallery/">The full gallery</a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="sect" aria-labelledby="made-title" data-reveal>
        <div class="sect__head">
          <p class="sect__num mono">IV.03</p>
          <h2 class="sect__title display" id="made-title">How a piece is made.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="steps" role="list">
          {
            steps.map((s, i) => (
              <li class="step">
                <span class="step__num display">0{i + 1}</span>
                <h3 class="step__title">{s.title}</h3>
                <p class="step__body">{s.body}</p>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="sect" aria-labelledby="cost-title" data-reveal>
        <div class="sect__head">
          <p class="sect__num mono">IV.04</p>
          <h2 class="sect__title display" id="cost-title">From $2,500. Larger pieces quoted.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sect__body prose-museum">
          <p>
            The base price covers a piece of roughly six to nine chapters with custom exhibits. Longer pieces, original
            illustration, data that needs cleaning, and voice or sound are quoted on the call. Half to start, half at
            launch. Hosted on your domain or mine; you own the files either way.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="sect" aria-labelledby="faq-title" data-reveal>
        <div class="sect__head">
          <p class="sect__num mono">IV.05</p>
          <h2 class="sect__title display" id="faq-title">Questions</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sect__body faq">
          {
            faq.map(({ q, a }) => (
              <div class="faq__item">
                <h3 class="faq__q">{q}</h3>
                <p class="faq__a">{a}</p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
          <p class="more faq__more">
            <a class="text-link" href="/what-is-a-scrolly/">What is a scrolly? &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="sect sect--close" aria-labelledby="close-title" data-reveal>
        <div class="sect__head">
          <p class="sect__num mono">IV.06</p>
          <h2 class="sect__title display" id="close-title">Bring the story. I will show you the page it becomes.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sect__body">
          <p class="lede">Thirty minutes. Leave with a chapter outline and a fixed quote.</p>
          {
            SCROLLY_INTAKE_URL && (
              <div class="intake">
                <iframe
                  class="intake__frame"
                  src={SCROLLY_INTAKE_URL}
                  title="Commission intake form"
                  loading="lazy"
                  referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
                />
                <p class="intake__alt">
                  <a class="text-link" href={SCROLLY_INTAKE_URL} rel="noopener">
                    Open the form on its own page
                  </a>
                </p>
              </div>
            )
          }
          <p class="actions">
            <a class:list={['cta', !SCROLLY_INTAKE_URL && 'cta--gilt']} href={SCHEDULER_URL}>Book a call</a>
            <a class="text-link actions__mail" href={mailto}>or write: {CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
  <Meander />
  <Colophon />
</Museum>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 5vw, 7rem);
  }
  .page__inner {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 4vw, 6rem);
  }
  .page__head,
  .sect {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 1rem + 4vw, 5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .page__statement {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.6rem;
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .page__statement .lede {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.9rem 1.4rem;
  }
  .actions__mail {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* Each room of the page: catalogue number and heading on the left, the matter on the right. */
  .sect {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2vw, 3rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .sect--wide {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.75rem, 1rem + 2vw, 2.5rem);
  }
  .sect__head {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    align-content: start;
  }
  .sect--wide .sect__head {
    max-width: 40rem;
  }
  .sect__num {
    color: var(--room-accent);
  }
  .sect__title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 1.4rem + 1.6vw, 2.6rem);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .sect__body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .sect--close .sect__body .lede {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* IV.06: the BackGold intake form, framed. The form is BackGold's own
     page, so it keeps its own type and colours inside the frame; it does
     not report its height, so the frame is tall and scrolls if it must. */
  .intake {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }
  .intake__frame {
    display: block;
    height: clamp(40rem, 110vh, 62rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    outline: 1px solid var(--gilt);
    outline-offset: 5px;
    margin: 6px;
    width: calc(100% - 12px);
    background: #fff;
  }
  .intake__alt {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  /* IV.01: the Room I feature-list cells. */
  .cells {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .cell {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    padding: 1.4rem 1.25rem 1.6rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--wall) 70%, white);
  }
  .cell__num {
    color: var(--gilt-ink);
  }
  .cell__title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .cell__body {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* IV.02: the gallery cards, then the way to the whole wall. */
  .more {
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  /* IV.05: the questions, one answer each, in the reading face. */
  .faq {
    gap: clamp(1.4rem, 1rem + 1.5vw, 2rem);
  }
  .faq__item {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    padding-top: 1.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .faq__item:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: 0;
  }
  .faq__q {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .faq__a {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .faq__more {
    padding-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  /* IV.03: three numbered steps. */
  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.6rem;
  }
  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    grid-template-areas:
      'num title'
      'num body';
    column-gap: 1rem;
    row-gap: 0.4rem;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--gilt);
  }
  .step__num {
    grid-area: num;
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--room-accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .step__title {
    grid-area: title;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .step__body {
    grid-area: body;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .page__head,
    .sect {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .cells {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .step {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      grid-template-areas:
        'num'
        'title'
        'body';
    }
  }
</style>
